{:org/id :org-global-freemasonry
 :org/form-family :family-fraternal-order
 :org/name "Freemasonry (regular and continental obediences)"
 :org/entity-kind :org-form
 :org/category :cat-fraternal
 :org/type :secular-community
 :org/scope :global
 :org/region-primary :region-europe
 :org/countries ["GB" "US" "FR" "BR" "PH" "IN"]
 :org/founding-date 1717
 :org/instance-count-estimate 100000
 :org/member-count-basis "partially source-pinned: the only firm figure available is one obedience's own — the United Grand Lodge of England reports ~170,000 members meeting in more than 7,000 lodges worldwide (of which ~20,000 are in overseas lodges). The commonly repeated worldwide total of ~6 million has NO authoritative census behind it: obediences do not publish comparable rolls, several do not recognize each other, and figures circulating range from about 2M to 6M. :org/member-count is therefore not asserted for world Freemasonry."
 :org/legal-registration :mixed
 :org/registration-note "Grand lodges are typically registered charities/corporations; individual lodges often are not, and membership rolls are private."
 :org/governance-model :hierarchical
 :org/mission-statement "Initiatory fraternal order structured by degrees, lodges and grand lodges, combining ritual, mutual aid and charity."
 :org/source-name "United Grand Lodge of England, About UGLE"
 :org/source-url "https://www.ugle.org.uk/about-us/about-ugle"
 :org/source-date "2025"
 :org/source-tier :primary
 :org/source-caveat "Primary for UGLE only. A world total would require summing self-declarations from mutually non-recognizing obediences, which is why no credible one exists."
 :org/pinned-on "2026-07-25"
 :org/data-provenance "source-pinned"
 :source/dataset "community-coverage"}

